# ── Credentials — never commit these ─────────────────────────────────────────
.env
*.json
# ...except this one: it's not a credential, it's ff_goalline's durable
# per-game de-dup manifest (which games have already been folded into the
# Off/Def season totals). Nothing regenerates it from scratch -- CI commits
# it back after every run so the Monday/Tuesday split doesn't double-count.
!ff_goalline/data/counted_games.json

# ── Virtual environment ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
env.bak/
venv.bak/

# ── Python cache ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[codz]
*$py.class
*.so

# ── Output CSVs (regenerated on each run) ────────────────────────────────────
*_adp.csv
combined_adp.csv
ff_draft_proj/*.csv
ff_projections/*.csv
ff_defense/*.csv
ff_defense/reddit_post.md
# ...except this one: it's Joe's hand-entered preseason defensive ranks,
# the prior that fetch_def_rating.py blends column H toward. Not
# regenerated by anything, so it has to be in the repo (CI needs it too).
!ff_defense/preseason_def_ranks.csv

# ── Raw source cache (~230MB of nflverse CSVs, re-fetchable) ─────────────────
# All of this is downloaded from nflverse's public releases on demand and is
# rebuilt by the fetchers, so it's cost with no benefit in history -- and
# pbp_2025.csv alone (94MB) is close enough to GitHub's 100MB per-file hard
# limit that committing it would eventually break a push outright.
ff_projections/cached/
ff_points_against/cached/
ff_idp_points_against/cached/
ff_utilization/cached/
ff_draft_proj/cached/
ff_goalline/cached/
ff_weekly_model/data/
ff_sfb16/historical_*.csv

# ── Long-form reference CSVs (regenerated on each fetch run) ─────────────────
ff_points_against/data/*.csv
ff_idp_points_against/data/*.csv

# Timestamped workbook backups — the live workbooks themselves are deliberately
# NOT ignored, since they hold hours of hand-entered usage that can't be
# regenerated and git history is worth having as a safety net. The dated
# copies beside them are just belt-and-braces and would bloat history.
ff_projections/*.backup-*.xlsx

# ── Probe/debug scripts (one-off helpers, not needed in repo) ─────────────────
probe_*.py
check_*.py

# ── Distribution / packaging ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
*.egg

# ── Testing ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ── OS junk ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Tools ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
ff_defense/nflverse_data/
ff_defense/nflverse_epa_exploration.xlsx
